# Default; no resources created. Do not put secret values in Terraform variables.
stage = "disabled"

# Later, after exact target / state / IAM review: "foundation",
# "runtime_private" or "runtime_public". Populate runtime_settings from
# reviewed private/public identifiers and PINNED secret VERSION NUMBERS only.

# DEV snapshot observation capability (default OFF): inside a complete, reviewed
# runtime_settings object, set read_metrics_enabled = true. This is a boolean;
# the JSON manifest uses true, not "true". Do not replace the other required fields.
# Omission/false leaves MYPAGE_READ_METRICS absent. Production rejects true.
# Changing this flag alone still does not authorize a serving update.
#
# To change an EXISTING serving DEV revision, use BOTH fields in the existing
# private settings for mypage-dev-plan AND mypage-dev-apply (not this example):
#   read_metrics_enabled       = true       # false to turn observation off
#   read_metrics_from_revision = "mypage-api-<observed-ready-revision>"
# The revision must be read from DEV, Ready, and receiving 100% of traffic.
# The Plan must contain exactly one service update: adding/removing the fixed
# MYPAGE_READ_METRICS=true env. Same image, origin, identity, secret versions,
# ingress, scaling and every other resource are required; drift/import/delete/
# replacement and unknown configuration are rejected. Other resources are no-op.
#
# Before enabling: build/deploy the #1437-capable image through the existing
# reviewed image release path, reconcile its State with a no-op Plan, and verify
# the exact runtime-release.json digest/source pair. This transition does not
# combine image rollout with logging, and cannot make an old image emit metrics.
# Verify the DEV apply identity already has the required update permission;
# do not expand IAM or bypass a rejected Plan as part of the toggle.
#
# Use the EXISTING runtime-private/public-plan and matching -apply workflow
# modes with exact source SHA. Independent Plan agreement, saved Plan hash,
# State-version binding and the 30-minute age limit remain mandatory.
# After apply, the readback step must verify a NEW ready revision, target env,
# unchanged configuration, generation progression and 100% traffic before
# accepting completion. Failure stops; it does not automatically roll back.
#
# Clear read_metrics_from_revision back to "" in both private settings after
# success, retaining the target read_metrics_enabled value, then confirm no-op.
# To disable/roll back, use false and the CURRENT newly observed ready revision
# in a fresh Plan/apply. Never replay the enable Plan or name an old revision.
# Keep synthetic measurement scope/limits, previous and new revision/digest,
# evidence and rollback together in the existing release record / Issue #1133.
# Inspect normal vs failed-query counters separately; returned docs != billed
# reads. This example does not perform deployment or prove live costs/readiness.
